h-mad/SKILL.md:3184:- `h_mad_audit_cycle.py` — audit-cycle verdict combiner: collects each pass from report-file transport or the always-armed `--out` fallback, gates delivered reports, and prints `AUDITCYCLE: PASS|FAIL|UNVERIFIED` + `[H-MAD]` marker, exit 0 on a verdict / 4 on operational error. `PASS` means all delivered passes gate cleanly; `FAIL` carries findings; `UNVERIFIED` means a pass produced no report, no gateable sections, a non-zero dispatch rc, or — since #13 — too little evidence to certify anything. `--pass` takes an optional 5th field, `i:<report>:<out>:<rc>[:<log>]`; when a log is given the render carries an **`Effort:`** block — per pass `tools=/ok=/failed=/thinking=`, and `low-evidence` when `ok` is at or below the 2 successful calls the report-file contract itself costs, i.e. the pass cannot have read anything (J49). **Since #13 it decides, in ONE direction only**: a pass at or below the floor can no longer certify a clean (`UNVERIFIED reason=low_evidence:pN`), and a named-but-unreadable log fails closed as `low_evidence_unmeasurable:pN` — a distinct token because the remedy differs, find the log versus re-dispatch the pass. It still cannot manufacture a `FAIL`; it is checked AFTER the findings loop, so findings a hollow pass did write still count, and after the rc loop, so a timeout explains itself rather than being reported as hollowness. A pass with **no log named** is NOT scored as hollow — that is the ordinary shape of a codex leg and of every `Agent()` teammate pass, and absence of measurement is not measurement of absence. The counts still never appear inside the `AUDITCYCLE:` token, only as the `reason=` field, and the `Effort:` block now renders on `UNVERIFIED` too, because those counts are the evidence FOR the verdict. **This reverses the rule that stood until 2026-09-04** ("it reports; it never decides"), by operator decision on measured evidence: the second surface was hollow in 21 of 22 passes on one feature, and on another produced 6 fabricated must-fixes of 11 against codex's 0 of 25, while its low-evidence passes never found anything in either direction. Honouring the delivery contract is not evidence of having read the tree. A named-but-unreadable log still renders as `unreadable` rather than as zeros — `tools=0` is exactly what a genuinely hollow pass looks like.
h-mad/SKILL.md:3258:- `h_mad_archreview_cycle.py` — Pass `--tree-snapshot <prompt>.tree.json` to `score` and treat `ARCHREVIEW-TREE: CHANGED` as a finding: “the review mutated what it measured”; this advisory never changes the recorded verdict or exit code. ONE Phase-6a-prime cycle, staged and scored: `stage` substitutes the reviewer template and prints the exact `exec agy` command, `score` runs the gates in the order that is the contract — **evidence FIRST, then verdict, then record, then READ BACK**. Prints `ARCHREVIEW: STAGED prompt=… base=… head=… bytes=N` or `ARCHREVIEW: READY_TO_MERGE|WITH_FIXES|NO tools=N recorded=yes` (exit 0), and `OVERSIZE`/`NO_EVIDENCE`/`LOW_EVIDENCE_CLEAN`/`NO_VERDICT`/`NOT_RECORDED`/`UNSUBSTITUTED`/`DEGENERATE_RANGE`/`UNREADABLE` (exit 2). **`OVERSIZE` refuses a prompt no delivery surface accepts and writes NO file** — `stage()` measured nothing while `h_mad_assemble_audit.py` held the measured ceiling one file over, so a ~690 KB prompt was staged, reported `STAGED`, and was then refused by the surface, which reads as "6a-prime failed" rather than "the prompt was never delivered"; the gate runs AFTER the output-contract prepend because that is the body a surface receives, and `--vh-tail N` is the remedy it names. **`LOW_EVIDENCE_CLEAN` is `NO_EVIDENCE` at the floor this channel's contract sets rather than at zero**: the reviewer template says "you must also WRITE your report file with `run_command`. That is the only write you may make" and asks for no `.done` marker, so `DELIVERY_FLOOR = 1` and a reviewer that read nothing but obeyed the delivery instruction used to score `tools=1` and pass. Derived from the CONTRACT, never from tool names — `h_mad_review_evidence.scan` knows none on purpose, and classifying calls as reads-vs-writes there would re-create the false zero that hardcoding `view_file|grep_search` produced. Asymmetric on purpose: only READY_TO_MERGE is held to the floor, because findings are evidence of reading and a clean is not, so a WITH_FIXES or NO at the same count is still recorded. `h_mad_audit_cycle.py` has carried `DELIVERY_FLOOR = 2` against the same J49 failure; this closes the asymmetry between the two channels. The seven mechanical steps of 6a-prime were hand-assembled **7 times in one session**, and the two with no other home are the two that get skipped: the BASE/HEAD stamp (a stale sha silently reviews the PREVIOUS commit — J41 one level up, which is why `DEGENERATE_RANGE` refuses `BASE == HEAD`) and the evidence gate (a dispatch whose single `view_file` errored returned `READY_TO_MERGE` in 1510 confident bytes, and rc, the extractor and the Phase-7 gate all took it). **`NO_EVIDENCE` and `NO_VERDICT` record NOTHING and carry no verdict word** — a review that read nothing has no verdict whatever its last line says, and recording it is what made that defect survivable. `NOT_RECORDED` exists because `archreview` is not in the schema's `required` array, so strict validation passes over a dropped write and the read-back is the only check. **One cycle per invocation: it does not decide whether to run another**, because that run went to seven when cycle 3 came back clean and cycle 4 then found a Critical vacuous pass. Deliberately NOT a variant of `audit-cycle`, which is a multi-pass verdict COMBINER over already-finished runs and rejects any phase outside plan/design/impl-plan — same word, different machine. Stdlib-only.
h-mad/SKILL.md:3268:- `h_mad_review_evidence.py` — 6a-prime evidence gate: `scan()` + CLI printing `EVIDENCE: PASS|NONE tools=N ok=K failed=J thinking=T [status=…]`, exit 0 on a verdict / 2 on `EVIDENCE: UNREADABLE reason=no_log|empty_log|unsupported_format`, which carries **no counts** so a cannot-judge cannot read as a zero. Answers only "did the review read anything" — never whether its findings are right. Counts any tool reaching `DONE`, knows no tool names, and reports `result.status` without gating on it. `thinking=` sums `usage.thinking_tokens` over completed `agent_response` steps and is reported for the same reason `status` is — triage, never a verdict (J49). With `--project-root <root>` the line (and the codex `CODEXEVIDENCE:` and grok lines) ends with `paths=N code=C other=O unmeasured=U`: the distinct EXISTING paths the calls named, split into code (under the root, outside its docs/ tree) and other (docs/ or outside the root), and the calls whose targets the transcript does not show (codex MCP calls print no arguments). Without a root the fields are absent, never zero, and they never change a verdict or an exit code. The audit-cycle driver threads its own root through, shows the same fields beside `tools=` in the `Effort:` block, records them in each pass's `.effort.json` sidecar, and copies the pass log to the project's `.h-mad/pass-logs/` directory under the collected report's name with its `log_sha256` (a failed copy records `log_retained: null` and a reason, and never costs the verdict). That directory writes its own `*` ignore file, and it is never pruned: each pass adds a full transcript (calibration logs ran 7–386 KB), so clear it by hand, for example at feature archive. Read `code=` as a floor: `other=` also carries the pass's own report file and its `.done` marker, and a `cd` inside one command line or a path quoted inside an inline `-c` script is not followed, so those calls read as zero targets rather than `unmeasured`. Stdlib-only.
