h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/evidence_targets.json:2:  "_why": "Skill-candidates row `the evidence gate counts tool CALLS, not their TARGETS` (LANDED 2026-10-05): the EVIDENCE/CODEXEVIDENCE lines and the audit-cycle Effort block carry paths=/code=/other=/unmeasured= beside tools= when a project root is given (absent, never zero, without one); agy run_command lines and codex exec blocks are shell-split and only EXISTING paths count; codex MCP calls (no arguments printed) are unmeasured; the split is code (under root, not docs/) vs other; the figures never change a verdict; the audit-cycle driver threads the root, records the figures in the effort sidecar, and COPIES the pass log to <root>/.h-mad/pass-logs/<collected>.log with its sha256, a copy failure being advisory. Each row breaks one of those properties.",
h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/wire_registry_key.json:44:      "_mechanism": "The original line, restored verbatim. A second feature's Task 4 evicts the first, and nothing anywhere reports it -- no tombstone, no provenance, no halt. This is the write that lost `audit-cycle-verb :: Task 4`.",
h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/archreview_oversize_halt.json:108:      "_mechanism": "The producer half of the contract that makes `failure-recovery.md`'s phase split correct. Edit this sentence out and phases 3/4/5b's bare `report-wait` hangs exactly as 6a-prime's did, with nothing to say so -- the review that found this called the sentence load-bearing and unpinned.",
h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/audit_stem_dir.json:2:  "_why": "Test-flake root cause 2026-10-05: a session fixture unlinked every /tmp/audit_*_run* file that appeared during the session, and /tmp is shared by every pytest session on the machine, other worktrees included, so one session deleted a concurrent session's live stems (`sed: /tmp/audit_handed-..._p2.asm.txt: No such file or directory`, random audit-cycle failures, BASELINE_NOT_GREEN under concurrent mutation runs). audit-cycle now stages under $HMAD_AUDIT_STEM_DIR (default /tmp, validated absolute, existing, colon-free), the conftest points it at the session's basetemp, and nothing sweeps /tmp. Each row breaks one of those properties.",
h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/stamp_written_is_this_run.json:2:  "_why": "`STAMP:` exists because seven live cycles emitted `AUDITCYCLE:` while their stamps were never written -- the two-round cap counted stamps and had none, and H3's `legs_changed` refusal could not fire. The token built to catch that decided with `is_file()`, which answers 'a stamp is there', not 'this run wrote one'. `_collected_path` is a pure function of feature/phase/cycle/index, so a re-run of the same cycle reads the PREVIOUS run's stamp: reproduced with a planted stale file, the run printed WRITTEN n=1 while the content stayed byte-identical and still named the earlier run. The mutations attack both directions -- back to existence, and over-corrected so nothing is ever WRITTEN -- because a guard that always cries ABSENT passes the stale-stamp test while making the token useless.",
h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/out_wait_atomicity.json:21:      "_mechanism": "Flip the opt-in and every existing report-wait caller silently loses the .done contract -- the one thing keeping a half-written report unreadable. Nobody asked for that, and nothing in their invocation would show it changed.",
h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/out_wait_atomicity.json:53:      "_mechanism": "The bug this helper shipped with for one suite run. `$$` is constant across every --out a single wrapper invocation writes, and audit-cycle writes one per pass -- so two writes share a temp and one clobbers the other. audit-cycle silently lost its p1 report. Fixing a race by adding a race.",
h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/report_path_handed.json:2:  "_why": "Skill-candidates row `a re-dispatched auditor gets a SUFFIXED report path, never the original's` (2026-10-05): two re-dispatched audit legs were handed the original legs' report paths, one clobber and one near-clobber, because both originals were alive and slow and were declared dead from a hook's Running: set (#49o). Claim once, never release (round 3), tightened in round 4: the assembler claims an absolute `--report-file` with an O_EXCL marker under $XDG_CACHE_HOME/h-mad/handed (keyed by realpath parent + casefolded name), refuses an existing report or prompt path, writes the prompt with O_EXCL, and derives --out from RP (appending `.txt` unless RP ends `.report.md`), refuses an --out that is RP; a reused path HALTs `report_path_handed` naming which was held and deletes nothing; `audit-cycle` mints a fresh stem per run. Each row breaks one of those properties.",

